{% extends "views/layouts/main.njk" %}

{% from "govuk/components/details/macro.njk" import govukDetails %}
{% from "govuk/components/inset-text/macro.njk" import govukInsetText %}

{% block pageTitle %}
	{{ pageHeading }} - {{ config.headerTitle }}
{% endblock %}

{#
	The user guide, as the team's "Identify Consultees user guide" doc has it. Contacts and
	timescales not agreed yet read "to be confirmed" - fill them in before go-live (README.md).
#}
{% set toBeConfirmed = "to be confirmed" %}

{% block pageContent %}
	<div class="govuk-grid-row">
		<div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
			<p class="govuk-body-l">
				Identify consultees finds the bodies to consult for a national infrastructure project: you pick the
				project, confirm its boundary, choose a ruleset, review the consultees it finds, and download a report pack.
			</p>

			<nav aria-label="Contents">
				<h2 class="govuk-heading-s">Contents</h2>
				<ul class="govuk-list">
					<li><a class="govuk-link" href="#before-you-start">Before you start</a></li>
					<li><a class="govuk-link" href="#step-by-step">Step by step</a></li>
					<li><a class="govuk-link" href="#report-pack">The report pack</a></li>
					<li><a class="govuk-link" href="#formatting-a-ruleset-change">Formatting a ruleset change</a></li>
					<li><a class="govuk-link" href="#requesting-a-ruleset-change">Requesting a ruleset change</a></li>
					<li><a class="govuk-link" href="#getting-help">Getting help</a></li>
				</ul>
			</nav>

			<h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="before-you-start">Before you start</h2>
			<p class="govuk-body">
				You sign in with your Planning Inspectorate Microsoft account, and your account must be in the
				service's access group.
			</p>
			<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
				<li>
					<strong>Getting access:</strong> ask to be added to the Identify consultees access group (who to ask is
					{{ toBeConfirmed }}). Without it, signing in ends on a page saying you do not have access.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Browser:</strong> any up-to-date browser. The maps need JavaScript; without it you see a still
					image of each map instead.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Projects:</strong> come from CBOS. A project appears once a case officer has uploaded its boundary
					shapefile to the case's GIS Shapefiles folder in CBOS and the cases have been imported since.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="step-by-step">Step by step</h2>
			<p class="govuk-body">A report takes 6 steps, from finding the project to downloading its pack.</p>
			<ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
				<li>
					<strong>Find the project.</strong> On the <a class="govuk-link" href="/">search page</a>, search by keyword,
					project reference or project title, or page through every project. Each row shows the project's stage in
					CBOS. Select the project's name.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Confirm the boundary.</strong> The project boundary page shows the site on a map. Under
					"Confirm shapefile for report", choose the boundary file to use - a project can have several, newest
					first - then select Continue.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Choose a ruleset.</strong> Pick the ruleset that applies to the project, then select Continue.
					England Wales post 30 April 2024 is selected unless you choose another.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Check the consultees.</strong> "Check consultees before creating the report" lists the report
					details - project, reference, shapefile and ruleset, each with a Change link - and every category of
					consultee found, with how many. The first run can take up to a minute for a large or detailed site.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Review each category.</strong> Select Change beside a category to see its consultees on a map
					and in a table, with why each was identified.
					<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
						<li>To take one out, select Remove and give a reason. It moves to "Removed consultees" with your reason.</li>
						<li>
							To add one the ruleset missed, select "Add a consultee", start typing its name, pick it from the
							suggestions and give a reason. Adding back a consultee you removed restores it.
						</li>
					</ul>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Create the report.</strong> On the check page, select Create report. On "Report created",
					download the report pack, a ZIP file.
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p class="govuk-body">
				Your additions and removals are kept in the page's web address, so a copied link to the check page brings
				them back. A ruleset run is reused for an hour; after that, the next page runs it again so newly loaded
				data is picked up.
			</p>
			{{ govukInsetText({
				text: "If a page says \"The ruleset could not be run\", no consultees are shown because the search did not finish. That is not the same as finding none - select Try again. A warning that the site was screened using its bounding box means the list can include consultees that are not near the site, so check each one."
			}) }}

			<h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="report-pack">The report pack</h2>
			<p class="govuk-body">
				The ZIP holds one Excel workbook and a PDF map for each category of consultee in the report. Before
				sending it, fill in "Report generated by" on the workbook's Summary tab - it is left blank and highlighted
				yellow for you.
			</p>
			<table class="govuk-table">
				<caption class="govuk-table__caption govuk-visually-hidden">What the report pack holds</caption>
				<thead class="govuk-table__head">
					<tr class="govuk-table__row">
						<th scope="col" class="govuk-table__header">Part</th>
						<th scope="col" class="govuk-table__header">What it holds</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody class="govuk-table__body">
					<tr class="govuk-table__row">
						<th scope="row" class="govuk-table__header">Summary tab</th>
						<td class="govuk-table__cell">
							The project, case reference, boundary file and when it was received, the ruleset, when the report was
							generated, "Report generated by" for you to fill in, a count per category, totals, the consultees added
							and removed with their reasons, and the national infrastructure projects (NSIPs) near the site
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr class="govuk-table__row">
						<th scope="row" class="govuk-table__header">A tab per group</th>
						<td class="govuk-table__cell">
							Administrative boundaries, Public bodies, Energy, Transport and Other: each consultee with its category,
							why it was identified and its source. Energy and Transport also show subcategory and distance from the site
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr class="govuk-table__row">
						<th scope="row" class="govuk-table__header">NSIPs tab</th>
						<td class="govuk-table__cell">
							Other projects within 35km of the site: name, number, type, sub-type and how each was found
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr class="govuk-table__row">
						<th scope="row" class="govuk-table__header">A PDF map per category</th>
						<td class="govuk-table__cell">
							The site, the category's consultees labelled on a grey basemap, and the ruleset's distances drawn dashed
							around the site, with a key and the consultees listed
						</td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
			<p class="govuk-body">
				Consultees you added show "Manually added", or your reason, in the workbook. Removed consultees are left out
				of the tabs and listed, with your reason, on the Summary tab. If the site was screened using its bounding
				box, the Summary says so.
			</p>

			<h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="formatting-a-ruleset-change">Formatting a ruleset change</h2>
			<p class="govuk-body">
				Each ruleset is one sheet of the rulesets workbook (Rulesets.xlsx), one row per condition, with exactly these
				6 columns in this order. Send the whole sheet with your change, not just the rows that changed.
			</p>
			<table class="govuk-table">
				<caption class="govuk-table__caption govuk-visually-hidden">The ruleset sheet's columns</caption>
				<thead class="govuk-table__head">
					<tr class="govuk-table__row">
						<th scope="col" class="govuk-table__header">Column</th>
						<th scope="col" class="govuk-table__header">What to put</th>
						<th scope="col" class="govuk-table__header">Allowed values</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody class="govuk-table__body">
					<tr class="govuk-table__row">
						<th scope="row" class="govuk-table__header">Group hierarchy</th>
						<td class="govuk-table__cell">The order of the group in the workbook</td>
						<td class="govuk-table__cell">A whole number (1, 2, 3 and so on)</td>
					</tr>
					<tr class="govuk-table__row">
						<th scope="row" class="govuk-table__header">Group</th>
						<td class="govuk-table__cell">Which report tab the consultee goes on</td>
						<td class="govuk-table__cell">Administrative boundaries, Public bodies, Energy, Transport or Other - anything else goes on Other</td>
					</tr>
					<tr class="govuk-table__row">
						<th scope="row" class="govuk-table__header">Category</th>
						<td class="govuk-table__cell">For administrative boundaries, the authority's role; blank otherwise</td>
						<td class="govuk-table__cell">A Bordering Authority, B Host Authority, C Host Authority, D Bordering Authority or Greater London Authority</td>
					</tr>
					<tr class="govuk-table__row">
						<th scope="row" class="govuk-table__header">Consultee Type(s)</th>
						<td class="govuk-table__cell">Which consultees, in words</td>
						<td class="govuk-table__cell">One of the accepted wordings, below</td>
					</tr>
					<tr class="govuk-table__row">
						<th scope="row" class="govuk-table__header">Logic</th>
						<td class="govuk-table__cell">How the consultee relates to the site</td>
						<td class="govuk-table__cell">Intersects application site, Intersects application site buffer or Borders host authority</td>
					</tr>
					<tr class="govuk-table__row">
						<th scope="row" class="govuk-table__header">Buffer (km)</th>
						<td class="govuk-table__cell">How far from the site, in kilometres</td>
						<td class="govuk-table__cell">0, unless Logic is Intersects application site buffer; then a number such as 1, 10 or 35</td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
			<p class="govuk-body">
				Wording is matched ignoring capitals and extra spaces, but otherwise must match exactly. A Consultee Type(s)
				wording not in the list needs a developer to map it to the data before the ruleset can go live, so say so in
				your request. The service will not start with an unrecognised wording, logic or buffer, so a mistake is caught
				before release rather than silently matching nothing.
			</p>
			{% set wordingsHtml %}
				<ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet">
					{% for wording in consulteeTypeWordings %}
						<li>{{ wording }}</li>
					{% endfor %}
				</ul>
				<p class="govuk-body">
					{{ awaitingDataWordings | join(", ") }} have no map data yet, so their conditions find nothing until it is loaded.
				</p>
			{% endset %}
			{{ govukDetails({
				summaryText: "Consultee Type(s) wordings accepted today (" ~ consulteeTypeWordings.length ~ ")",
				html: wordingsHtml
			}) }}
			<p class="govuk-body">
				A new ruleset is a new sheet. Give it a name with any date it applies from, such as "England Wales post 30
				April 2024", and say whether it should become the default.
			</p>

			<h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="requesting-a-ruleset-change">Requesting a ruleset change</h2>
			<p class="govuk-body">
				Ruleset changes are made by D&amp;D, and a change reaches the live service only after you have checked it on
				the test environment.
			</p>
			{% include "views/help/change-flow.svg.njk" %}
			<ol class="govuk-list govuk-list--number">
				<li>
					<strong>You edit the sheet.</strong> Change the ruleset's sheet in Rulesets.xlsx following the formatting
					rules above. Note what changed, why, and the date it should apply from.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>You send the request</strong> to D&amp;D (contact details {{ toBeConfirmed }}), with the sheet attached. Mark it
					urgent only if a live report would otherwise be wrong.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>D&amp;D triages it.</strong> They check the wording against the accepted list. A new Consultee
					Type(s) wording, or a consultee type with no map data yet, takes longer: the data has to be found and
					loaded first.
				</li>
				<li><strong>D&amp;D makes and tests the change</strong>, then deploys it to the test environment.</li>
				<li>
					<strong>You check it on test.</strong> Run 1 or 2 projects you know well through the changed ruleset and
					confirm the consultees are as expected. Reply "approved", or say what needs changing.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>D&amp;D releases it</strong> to the training and live services, and tells you when it is live.
				</li>
			</ol>
			<table class="govuk-table">
				<caption class="govuk-table__caption govuk-table__caption--s">How long a change takes</caption>
				<thead class="govuk-table__head">
					<tr class="govuk-table__row">
						<th scope="col" class="govuk-table__header">Kind of change</th>
						<th scope="col" class="govuk-table__header">Example</th>
						<th scope="col" class="govuk-table__header">Timescale</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody class="govuk-table__body">
					{% for change in [
						["Acknowledging a request", "Any request"],
						["A wording or distance change using accepted wordings", "Hospitals within 10km becomes 15km"],
						["A new ruleset sheet", "A ruleset for a new legislative date"],
						["A new Consultee Type(s) wording for existing data", "A new name for an existing type"],
						["A new consultee type needing new data", "MoD safeguarding areas"],
						["An urgent fix to a live ruleset", "A condition matching the wrong bodies"]
					] %}
						<tr class="govuk-table__row">
							<th scope="row" class="govuk-table__header">{{ change[0] }}</th>
							<td class="govuk-table__cell">{{ change[1] }}</td>
							<td class="govuk-table__cell">{{ toBeConfirmed | capitalize }}</td>
						</tr>
					{% endfor %}
				</tbody>
			</table>

			<h2 class="govuk-heading-l" id="getting-help">Getting help</h2>
			<p class="govuk-body">
				Most problems clear with Try again. If one does not, contact the service team (contact details
				{{ toBeConfirmed }}) with the project reference and what the page said.
			</p>
			<table class="govuk-table">
				<caption class="govuk-table__caption govuk-visually-hidden">Common problems and what to do</caption>
				<thead class="govuk-table__head">
					<tr class="govuk-table__row">
						<th scope="col" class="govuk-table__header">What you see</th>
						<th scope="col" class="govuk-table__header">What to do</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody class="govuk-table__body">
					<tr class="govuk-table__row">
						<th scope="row" class="govuk-table__header">The project is not in the search</th>
						<td class="govuk-table__cell">
							Check its boundary shapefile is uploaded to the case's GIS Shapefiles folder in CBOS, then ask an admin to
							import cases from CBOS
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr class="govuk-table__row">
						<th scope="row" class="govuk-table__header">No stage beside a project</th>
						<td class="govuk-table__cell">Ask an admin to import cases from CBOS again</td>
					</tr>
					<tr class="govuk-table__row">
						<th scope="row" class="govuk-table__header">The ruleset could not be run</th>
						<td class="govuk-table__cell">Select Try again. A very large site can take up to a minute</td>
					</tr>
					<tr class="govuk-table__row">
						<th scope="row" class="govuk-table__header">A bounding box warning</th>
						<td class="govuk-table__cell">Check each consultee, and remove any that do not apply</td>
					</tr>
					<tr class="govuk-table__row">
						<th scope="row" class="govuk-table__header">A consultee you expected is missing</th>
						<td class="govuk-table__cell">
							Add it by hand with a reason, and request a ruleset change if it should always be found. Some types
							have no data yet: MoD areas, coal mining areas and the Cheshire brine area
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr class="govuk-table__row">
						<th scope="row" class="govuk-table__header">The report pack will not download</th>
						<td class="govuk-table__cell">Select Retry download</td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</div>
{% endblock %}
